<p>Boston is one of the priciest cities in the country, and that cuts both ways. Rent stings, but people here also pay a real premium for anyone who is skilled, punctual and trustworthy. That's why the best side hustles in Boston lean toward expertise — tutoring, childcare, skilled home help, freelancing for biotech and universities — with gig apps filling the gaps.</p>
<p>Below are 18 side gigs in Boston, what each typically pays, what it takes to start, and how to time them around the city's very particular calendar: September 1 move-in chaos, Marathon Monday, the Head of the Charles, and a winter that reliably delivers snow.</p>

