<h2 id="how-to-start">How to start a side hustle in Boston this month</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Pick a gig that uses something you already have.</strong> A degree, a car, a strong back, a love of dogs. Skills earn premium rates in Boston.</li>
  <li><strong>Price for Boston, not national averages.</strong> Use the <a href="/tools/freelance-rate-calculator/">freelance rate calculator</a> so your rate actually covers taxes and time.</li>
  <li><strong>List in the right places.</strong> Gig apps for driving and delivery; Care.com, Nextdoor, parent groups, campus job boards and Google Business Profile for local services.</li>
  <li><strong>File a business certificate if you use a brand name.</strong> It's a one-page form with the City Clerk, and it lets you open a business bank account.</li>
  <li><strong>Book the seasonal rushes early.</strong> Line up September moving jobs in July and snow clients in October.</li>
  <li><strong>Save for taxes from day one.</strong> Put 25–30% of profit aside in a separate account.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="massachusetts-taxes">Massachusetts taxes and rules for side income</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>State income tax:</strong> a flat 5% on most income. A 4% surtax applies only to income above an inflation-adjusted threshold ($1,107,750 for 2026), so it won't touch most side hustlers.</li>
  <li><strong>No city income tax:</strong> Boston doesn't levy its own income tax.</li>
  <li><strong>Self-employment tax:</strong> 15.3% federal on net profit plus federal income tax. Estimate your set-aside with the <a href="/tools/self-employment-tax-calculator/">self-employment tax calculator</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Sales tax:</strong> 6.25% on most physical goods. Register with the Department of Revenue if you sell products; most personal services aren't taxed.</li>
  <li><strong>Business certificate:</strong> required if you operate under a name other than your legal name — $65 at Boston City Hall, renewed every four years.</li>
  <li><strong>Rideshare rules:</strong> drivers must pass a state background check in addition to the app's own screening.</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Watch out:</strong> Short-term rental hosting in Boston is tightly restricted and requires city registration. Read the city's rules before listing a room or co-hosting for someone else.</div>

